  "reasoning": "The defendant, a government animal health inspector, abused his official position to issue false official documents (27 copies of a prohibited animal product certificate). This constitutes forging or altering state-issued documents, which matches the charge '伪造、变造、买卖国家机关公文、证件、印章'. By providing these false documents, he enabled others to obtain state subsidy funds through deception, which also fits the definition of fraud ('诈骗'). Therefore both charges apply.",
  "final_answer": "伪造、变造、买卖国家机关公文、证件、印章;诈骗"
